#[summary("구조체만으로 된 재귀: 정해지지 않은 정렬과 필드 사실 (ADR-0047 §3, backlog 2O-03d)")]
mod rs {
    struct Node { v: i64, kids: Vec<Node> }

    // Mutual recursion through two structs.
    struct Dir { name: u64, subs: Vec<Dir>, files: Vec<File> }

    struct File { size: u64, links: Vec<Dir> }

    struct Rose<T> { v: T, kids: Vec<Rose<T>> }

    // An enum holding a recursive struct.
    enum Slot { Empty, Full(Node) }

    spec fn bare(n: &Node, x: i64) -> bool { n.v == x && n.kids.len() == 0 }

    spec fn small(n: &Node) -> bool { n.kids.len() < 100 }

    spec fn adopted(a: &Node, b: &Node, c: &Node) -> bool {
        b.kids.len() == a.kids.len() + 1 && b.v == a.v && b.kids[a.kids.len()].v == c.v
    }

    spec fn first_is(n: &Node, x: i64) -> bool { n.kids.len() > 0 && n.kids[0].v == x }

    // The depth along first children, a recursive spec fn.
    spec fn spine(n: &Node) -> i64
        decreases n,
    {
        if n.kids.len() == 0 { 0 } else { 1 + spine(&n.kids[0]) }
    }

    spec fn spine_ok(n: &Node) -> bool { spine(n) >= 0 }

    #[effects(pure)]
    #[uses(bare)]
    fn leaf(x: i64) -> (r: Node)
        ensures bare(&r, x),
    {
        Node { v: x, kids: Vec::new() }
    }

    #[effects(pure)]
    #[uses(small, adopted)]
    fn adopt(n: &mut Node, c: Node) -> ()
        requires small(n),
        ensures adopted(old(n), n, &c),
    {
        n.kids.push(c);
    }

    // A write two levels down.
    #[effects(pure)]
    #[uses(first_is)]
    fn relabel_first(n: &mut Node, x: i64) -> ()
        requires first_is(n, 0),
        ensures first_is(n, x),
    {
        n.kids[0].v = x;
    }

    #[effects(pure)]
    fn total(n: &Node) -> i64
        decreases n,
    {
        let mut i: usize = 0;
        let mut s: i64 = n.v;
        while i < n.kids.len()
            invariant i <= n.kids.len(),
            decreases n.kids.len() - i,
        {
            s = s.wrapping_add(total(&n.kids[i]));
            i = i + 1;
        }
        s
    }

    #[effects(pure)]
    fn files(d: &Dir) -> u64
        decreases d,
    {
        let mut n: u64 = 0;
        for i in 0..d.subs.len()
            invariant i <= d.subs.len(),
        {
            n = n.wrapping_add(files(&d.subs[i]));
        }
        n.wrapping_add(u64::try_from(d.files.len()).unwrap())
    }

    #[effects(pure)]
    fn size<T>(r: &Rose<T>) -> u64
        decreases r,
    {
        let mut n: u64 = 1;
        for i in 0..r.kids.len()
            invariant i <= r.kids.len(),
        {
            n = n.wrapping_add(size::<T>(&r.kids[i]));
        }
        n
    }

    #[effects(pure)]
    #[uses(spine, spine_ok)]
    fn spine_len(n: &Node) -> u64
        ensures spine_ok(n),
        decreases n,
    {
        if n.kids.len() == 0 { 0 } else { spine_len(&n.kids[0]).wrapping_add(1) }
    }

    #[effects(pure)]
    #[uses(bare)]
    fn slot_value(s: &Slot) -> i64 {
        match s {
            Slot::Empty => 0,
            Slot::Full(n) => n.v,
        }
    }

    #[effects(pure)]
    #[uses(bare, small, adopted, first_is)]
    fn build() -> i64 {
        let mut root: Node = leaf(1);
        adopt(&mut root, leaf(0));
        relabel_first(&mut root, 7);
        root.kids[0].v
    }
}
